- The install engine (vilna-installer-engine, as root through sudo
  after the Herkos screen): systemd-repart copies the system partition
  of the Vilna disk image block by block into LUKS2 (recovery key, TPM2
  or a passphrase, as Aeon), the btrfs grows to the disk and gets a
  UUID of its own, the model is copied and checked with sha256sum,
  languages, keyboards, time zone, computer name, the account and the
  Wi-Fi connection are set up, and sdbootutil installs the boot loader
